# CombatMode Architecture and Style

Use this project map and conventions for all changes.

## Runtime structure

- `CombatMode/CombatMode.toc`: addon metadata, `SavedVariables: CombatModeDB`, load order entrypoint.
- `CombatMode/Embeds.xml`: loads Lua files and owns the root frame scripts (`OnEvent`, `OnUpdate` bridge).
- `CombatMode/Constants/*.lua`: constants and static tables (`CM.Constants`; `Namespace.lua` first).
- `CombatMode/Core/{Runtime,FreeLook,Crosshair,ClickCasting,PartyRadial}/`: runtime systems and gameplay behavior by domain.
- `CombatMode/UI/Options/*.lua`: standalone custom options window (`CM.UI` toolkit + tabs).
- `CombatMode/UI/Changelog/*.lua`: in-game changelog viewer (namespace + data + panel).
- `CombatMode/UI/Editors/*.lua`: standalone secondary editor windows (Reticle CVar, Targeting Macro Prelines).
- `CombatMode/Bindings.xml`: keybinding declarations and binding click targets.

## Module responsibilities

- `Core/Runtime/Runtime.lua`: owns the AddOn namespace table (`local addonName, CM = ...`), optional `_G.CM` debug alias, native SavedVariables (`CombatModeDB` → `CM.DB.global` / `CM.DB.char`), slash commands, lifecycle (`ADDON_LOADED` → `OnInitialize`, `PLAYER_LOGIN` → `OnEnable`), cross-feature coordination points, global `CombatMode_OnUpdate`, the first-login welcome modal (deferred `CM.UI.ShowWelcome` with `CM.Constants.PopupMsg`), deferred in-game changelog open (`ScheduleChangelogIfNewVersion` → `CM.Config.MaybeShowChangelogOnNewVersion`) when `CM.DB.global.lastSeenChangelogVersion` ≠ `CM.METADATA["VERSION"]` (always when Debug Mode is on), and `CM.UninstallCombatMode` (options sidebar Uninstall button: restore prior CVars, reset left/right click camera binds, disable addon, reload). `OnResetDB` wipes settings but preserves the prior CVar snapshot. Registers Blizzard events on `CombatModeFrame` during enable.
- `Core/Runtime/EventRouter.lua`: owns centralized event category dispatch and `_G.CombatMode_OnEvent`; builds/owns `eventCategoryMap`.
- `Core/Runtime/CVarManager.lua`: owns all addon-owned **CVar writes** (centralized `CM.SetCVar*` helpers), pre-CM **priorCVarSnapshot** capture/restore (`CM.CapturePriorCVarSnapshot` at each enable before writes, `CM.EnsurePriorCVarSnapshot` as a mid-session no-op safety net, `CM.RestorePriorCVars` on Uninstall), and the feature-level CVar helpers (reticle targeting presets merged with `CM.DB.global.reticleTargetingCVarOverrides` via `CM.GetEffectiveReticleTargetingCVarValues`, Interaction HUD soft-target subset, action camera, sticky crosshair, shoulder offset, mouselook speed). Uninstall prefers restoring the session snapshot over hard-coded Blizzard tables.
- `Core/Runtime/BindingQueue.lua`: owns combat-safe deferred binding write queue (`CM.TryApplyBindingChange`, `CM.FlushDeferredBindingChanges`).
- `Core/Runtime/Bootstrap.lua`: owns startup wiring (`CM.BootstrapFeatureModules`) and `CM.RestorePriorBindings` (Uninstall resets `BUTTON1`/`BUTTON2` to Blizzard camera defaults only).
- `Core/FreeLook/FreeLookController.lua`: owns free-look/mouselook state transitions, cursor-mode keybind behavior, and UI side effects tied to lock/unlock flow. Lock applies centering with force-CVar-0 → `MouselookStart` → deferred CVar-1 (PartyRadial / 10.2 quirk). OPie close rematch is latched via `CM.NotifyOpieUnlockFrameVisible` / `CM.RematchFreeLookAfterOpieIfNeeded` from Runtime OnUpdate so a ring that stops mouselook and frees centering cannot leave mouselook on with a visible cursor.
- `Core/FreeLook/AutoCursorUnlock.lua`: owns unlock predicates (frame visibility, mounts, pet battle, custom expression) and wildcard frame tracking.
- `Constants/Namespace.lua`: initializes the `CM.Constants` namespace only.
- `Constants/{CVars,Assets,Gameplay,DatabaseDefaults,PartyRadial,FrameWatch,Reticle}.lua`: define immutable/static tables (defaults, CVars, event groups, assets, watchlists, radial metadata); no runtime side effects beyond table population.
- `Core/Crosshair/Crosshair.lua`: owns crosshair visuals and reaction logic. Crosshair reaction and cursor centering follow `CM.IsCrosshairEnabled()`. `CM.SetCrosshairOptionsPreview(enabled)` / `CM.IsCrosshairPreviewActive()` force the crosshair (and the Interaction HUD + Combat Assist companions) to render outside their normal mouselook/combat conditions for the Crosshair options tab. Vertical position is account-wide `CM.DB.global.crosshairY` (options slider only).
- `Core/Crosshair/InteractionHUD.lua`: owns the Interaction HUD widget lifecycle, fade/range `OnUpdate`, and soft-interact event handling.
- `Core/Crosshair/AssistedHighlight.lua`: owns Assisted Combat suggestion icon + keybind near the crosshair.
- `Core/Crosshair/Animations.lua`: owns user-facing animations (cursor pulse after unlock/free-look transitions; crosshair reaction/lock-in presentation).
- `Core/ClickCasting/BindingOverrides.lua`: owns override binding/macro synthesis for mouse buttons and modified clicks; refreshes when bars/bindings change.
- `Core/ClickCasting/AddonActionBarResolver.lua`: owns third-party action bar button resolution by action-slot id (ElvUI/Bartender4).
- `Core/ClickCasting/TargetingMacroBuilder.lua`: owns reticle-targeting macro text construction (pre-line, /click wrapper, @cursor handling). Exports `CM.TargetingMacroPrelinesDefaults`; honors account-wide `CM.DB.global.targetingMacroPrelineAnyOverride` / `targetingMacroPrelineEnemyOverride` when set.
- `Core/PartyRadial/PartyRadial.lua`: owns radial frame lifecycle, selection tracking, secure cast attributes, and group/role slice updates. Exposed as `CM.PartyRadial` (API name kept for call-site/DB stability). `CM.PartyRadial.SetOptionsPreview(enabled)` / `IsOptionsPreviewActive()` force a layout-only radial (no freelook unlock, no `IsActive`) for the Party Radial options tab; empty slots use placeholders; Visual Settings refresh via `ApplyVisualConfig`.
- `UI/Options/Draw.lua`: owns the theme tokens (`CM.UI.Colors` / `UI.Fonts` / `UI.Radius` — a minimal neutral-grey ramp with a single accent yellow), `UI.StripColors` / `UI.SetFontSize`, drawing primitives (rounded surfaces, circular knob mask, font sizing, ESC-close, drag helpers), and the themed config tooltip (`UI.ShowTooltip` / `UI.HideTooltip` / `UI.AttachTooltip` via `CombatModeUITooltip`, not `GameTooltip`). Visuals only. Text renders at `UI.Fonts.base` with inline `|cff..|` markup stripped; only `UI.MakeHeader` uses `UI.Fonts.header` + accent; option rows use a 60/40 split (title + muted `opts.desc` helper in the left column; control in the right, vertically centered).
- `UI/Options/Widgets.lua`: owns the control factories (toggle, slider, dropdown via `MenuUtil`, keybind capture, text/multiline input, pill button, header, description). Shared helpers for sibling modules: `CM.UI.Options.RegisterControl` / `IsDisabled` / `AttachOptionText` / `AddRowHover`. Every value control exposes `:Refresh()` and registers with `CM.UI.Options` for the central `Options.Sync()` pass; `UI.Confirm(text, onAccept)` / `UI.Notify(text, onClose)` own the themed modal (`CombatModeConfirmDialog`) — one shared window built from the `Draw.lua` primitives that replaces Blizzard's `StaticPopup`, with a logo + wordmark header, full-screen click blocker, ESC cancel, and colors stripped from the message. `Confirm` shows paired Yes/No and fires `onAccept` on Yes only; `Notify` collapses to a single centered Okay and fires `onClose` on any dismissal. Toggles and buttons that pass `confirm = true` route their apply step through `UI.Confirm`. `UI.ShowWelcome` owns the dedicated first-install modal `CombatModeWelcomeDialog` (not registered in `UISpecialFrames`, so load-end `CloseSpecialWindows` cannot dismiss it).
- `UI/Options/SpellMultiSelect.lua`: owns `UI.MakeSpellMultiSelect` (spellbook + ID suggestions, icon+name pills, CSV get/set for Reticle Targeting spell lists).
- `UI/Options/OptionsPanel.lua`: owns `CombatModeOptionsFrame` (standalone movable window, sidebar tabs, scroll content), the vertical layout manager (`ctx`), `CM.OpenOptions`/`CM.ToggleOptions`/`CM.CloseOptions` (combat-guarded), `CM.GetOptionsFrame`, and the reusable `CM.UI.CreateWindow` / `CM.UI.NewLayout` used by editors. `CM.UI.Options.AddTab` is the tab registration entry point. The window docks left-of-center on open (`Options.DockWindowLeft`) so the crosshair and party radial stay clear for live previews. The bottom of the sidebar hosts a fixed footer (`BuildSidebarFooter`) with the Silence Alerts / Debug Mode toggles and the View Changelog / Reset to Defaults / Uninstall buttons (formerly the About tab).
- `UI/Options/BlizzardSettingsBridge.lua`: registers a Blizzard AddOns canvas category (Escape → Options → AddOns → Combat Mode) whose only control opens `CM.OpenOptions`; does not host settings itself.
- `UI/Options/Tabs/Tab*.lua`: per-category tab builders (General, Crosshair, ReticleTargeting, ClickCasting, AutoCursorUnlock, Camera, PartyRadial). Each calls `CM.UI.Options.AddTab` and wires get/set/disabled closures to existing `CM.*` feature APIs + `CM.DB` fields (no duplicated feature logic). Tab defs may add `onSelect`/`onDeselect` for transient side effects (fired in pairs on tab switch and window show/hide); `TabCrosshair.lua` uses them to call `CM.SetCrosshairOptionsPreview(true)` so the real crosshair, Interaction HUD, and Combat Assist icon preview live with mouselook off; `TabPartyRadial.lua` uses them to call `CM.PartyRadial.SetOptionsPreview(true)` so the Party Radial previews Visual Settings live.
- `UI/Changelog/ChangelogNamespace.lua`: initializes the `CM.Config` namespace only.
- `UI/Changelog/ChangelogData.lua`: holds `CM.Config.ChangelogText` (markdown string for the in-game viewer); keep in sync with `CombatMode/CHANGELOG.md` via `scripts/sync-changelog-to-lua.ps1`.
- `UI/Changelog/ChangelogPanel.lua`: changelog popup UI (`SimpleHTML` + `ScrollFrame`); `CM.Config.ShowChangelog`, `CM.Config.MaybeShowChangelogOnNewVersion`; sets `CM.DB.global.lastSeenChangelogVersion` when shown. Called from the sidebar footer (View Changelog) and scheduled in `Core/Runtime/Runtime.lua` on login after version changes.
- `UI/Editors/ReticleCVarEditorData.lua`: reticle CVar editor row data and override persistence helpers.
- `UI/Editors/ReticleCVarEditorPanel.lua`: custom Reticle Targeting CVar editor UI; `CM.OpenReticleTargetingCVarEditor()`; anchors to the right of `CM.GetOptionsFrame()` when open.
- `UI/Editors/TargetingMacroPrelinesEditor.lua`: standalone custom window (built on the `CM.UI` toolkit) for click-cast preline overrides; `CM.OpenTargetingMacroPrelinesEditor()`; opened from the Reticle Targeting tab.

## Required coding conventions

- **Lua global localization header convention**
  - Keep global aliases per-file; do not create a shared/global alias module (for example, no `CM.API` globals table).
  - Header order:
    1. AddOn namespace handle (`local _, CM = ...`; Runtime uses `local addonName, CM = ...`) and `_G` when needed
    2. WoW API globals
    3. Lua stdlib aliases (`pairs`, `ipairs`, `type`, `pcall`, `math`, etc.)
    4. module-local constants
    - Localize only symbols used in that file.
    - Remove unused aliases when touching a file.
    - Prefer function alias style (`local strfind = _G.string.find`) unless many members from the table are used.
    - Do not use `local CM = _G.CM` — the shared table comes from `...`. `_G.CM` is an optional debug alias only.
- Keep event wiring centralized via constants and core dispatch; avoid ad-hoc event frames.
- Prefer extending existing `CM` feature APIs over introducing new global state.
- Respect combat lockdown and secure action patterns (`SecureActionButtonTemplate`, macro attributes).
- Use existing DB scopes consistently:
  - account-wide in `CM.DB.global`
  - character-specific in `CM.DB.char`
- Put new user-facing settings in the matching `UI/Options/Tabs/Tab*.lua` builder (call `ctx:Toggle/Slider/Dropdown/...` with get/set/disabled closures); add a new tab via `CM.UI.Options.AddTab`.
- Preserve slash command and keybinding behavior unless change is explicitly requested.
- Lua validation default is changed-files pre-commit: `pre-commit run --files <changed files>`.
- Use direct formatter/linter commands only for targeted debugging.
- Run repo-wide gate only for release prep or explicit maintainer request: `pre-commit run --all-files`.

## Change expectations

- Follow current file header purpose comments as source of truth for module intent.
- Keep edits minimal and local to the owning module.
- Call out behavior changes that affect mouselook, targeting CVars, or binding overrides.
